{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--no-independent-adjective-word-class","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu lacks an independent word class of adjectives, and concepts corresponding to adjectives are classified as intransitive verbs.","ja":"アイヌ語には独立した形容詞という品詞は存在せず、形容詞に相当する概念は自動詞として分類される。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0007-09","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2015@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0002-07","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0097-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0114-12","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0121-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0036-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0019-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--property-words-share-intransitive-person-affixes","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--person-marking-frame"],"statement":{"en":"Property-concept words take the exact same set of subject person-marking affixes as intransitive verbs.","ja":"属性概念を表す語は自動詞とまったく同一の主語人称標識接辞をとる。"},"type":"paradigm-cell","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["ku-","-as","e-","es-","eci-","-an"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0091-05","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0116-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0023-12","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--no-independent-adjective-word-class","differs_in":null,"note":"The complete identity in subject person-marking between property words and intransitive verbs provides key morphosyntactic evidence against an independent adjective class."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--stative-verbs-express-inchoative-change","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--stative-inchoative"],"statement":{"en":"Stative property verbs in Ainu inherently express both a state and an inchoative change into that state without morphological derivation.","ja":"アイヌ語の状態動詞（性質語）は、形態的派生を伴わずに状態とその状態への起動相的変化の双方を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["poro","hure","pirka"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0116-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0121-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0434-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0018-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--property-verbs-reject-inchoative-ne","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--stative-inchoative"],"statement":{"en":"Stative property verbs cannot combine with the copula ne to express inchoative change because inchoative meaning is already inherent in the stem.","ja":"状態動詞（性質語）は語幹自体で状態変化を表すため、変化を表すためにコピュラ ne と共起することはできず非文法的となる。"},"type":"judgement","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["ne","poro","hure"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0091-08","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0116-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--stative-verbs-express-inchoative-change","differs_in":null,"note":"The ungrammaticality of *X ne demonstrates that the stative stem itself already encodes change of state."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--adjectives-lack-imperative-as-sole-distinction","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--standard-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Adjectives lack an imperative form, which functions as the only morphological and functional distinction separating them from verbs.","ja":"形容詞には命令形が存在せず、この点が動詞と形容詞を分ける唯一の形態的・機能的相違点である。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0106-05","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0020-04","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--stative-verbs-express-inchoative-change","differs_in":"framework","note":"The traditional claim that adjectives categorically lack imperatives contrasts with the stative-inchoative analysis, under which property verbs can form imperatives in their inchoative reading."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-adjectival-suffix-an-originally-a-verb-meaning","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The adjectival suffix -an, originally a verb meaning 'to exist', forms adjectives from nouns and also forms demonstrative and interrogative adjectives from pronouns.","ja":"形容詞語尾 -an は元来「ある」意の動詞であり、名詞から形容詞を派生するほか、指示代名詞や疑問代名詞から指示形容詞や疑問形容詞をつくる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-an"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0139-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-suffix-ash-forms-adjectives-describing-physical-or","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The suffix -ash forms adjectives describing physical or personal attributes from body-part and related nouns.","ja":"接尾辞 -ash は身体部位などの名詞から属性を表す形容詞をつくる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-ash"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0139-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-adjectival-suffix-ush-is-historically-the-plural","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The adjectival suffix -ush is historically the plural of -un.","ja":"形容詞語尾 -ush は歴史的には -un の複数形に由来する。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-ush","-un"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0139-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-adjectival-suffix-o-originally-a-verb-meaning","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The adjectival suffix -o, originally a verb meaning 'to be inside' or 'to be attached to', forms adjectives from nouns.","ja":"形容詞語尾 -o は元来「はいっている」「ついている」意の動詞であり、名詞から形容詞をつくる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-o"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0140-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-suffix-nu-attaches-to-nouns-to-mean","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The suffix -nu attaches to nouns to mean 'abundant in', and it can attach to -ash adjectives to intensify their meaning.","ja":"接尾辞 -nu は名詞に付いて「…が多い」意の形容詞をつくり、また -ash 形容詞に付いてその意味を強める。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-nu","-ashnu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0140-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-adjectival-suffix-ne-originally-a-verb-meaning","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The adjectival suffix -ne, originally a verb meaning 'to be', developed from the sense of '-shaped' or 'like...' into a widely used adjective suffix.","ja":"形容詞語尾 -ne は元来「である」意味の動詞であり、「……状の」「……のような」の意味から広く形容詞語尾となった。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0140-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-adjectival-suffix-kor-originally-a-verb-meaning","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The adjectival suffix -kor, originally a verb meaning 'to have', forms adjectives indicating possession of a quality or feature.","ja":"形容詞語尾 -kor は元来「もつ」意の動詞であり、性質や特徴を有することを表す形容詞をつくる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0141-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-adjectival-suffix-sak-originally-a-verb-meaning","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The adjectival suffix -sak, originally a verb meaning 'to lack', forms privative adjectives.","ja":"形容詞語尾 -sak は元来「を缺く」意の動詞であり、欠如を表す形容詞をつくる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-sak"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0141-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-adjectival-suffix-nak-is-derived-historically-from","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The adjectival suffix -nak is derived historically from -sak.","ja":"形容詞語尾 -nak は歴史的に -sak に由来する。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-nak","-sak"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0141-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-adjectival-suffix-ke-forms-adjectives-from-noun","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The adjectival suffix -ke forms adjectives from noun roots or onomatopoetic stems.","ja":"接尾辞 -ke は名詞語根や擬声語語幹などから形容詞をつくる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-ke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0141-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-suffix-no-imparts-the-meaning-well-or","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The suffix -no imparts the meaning 'well' or 'proficiently' in deriving adjectives from verbs.","ja":"接尾辞 -no は動詞に「よく」の意を添えて形容詞をつくる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-no"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0141-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-suffix-ko-attaches-to-adjectives-to-impart","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The suffix -ko attaches to adjectives to impart an opposite meaning.","ja":"接尾辞 -ko は形容詞に付いて反対の意味を添える。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-ko"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0142-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-ending-ma-functions-as-an-adjective-ending","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The ending -ma functions as an adjective ending, as seen in tuima 'distant', ramma 'constant', and moshma 'other'.","ja":"語尾 -ma は形容詞語尾として機能し、tuima「遠い」、ramma「常住の」、moshma「他の」などに見られる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-ma","tuima","ramma","moshma"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0180-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-ending-tek-forms-property-verbs-adjectives-as","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs"],"statement":{"en":"The ending -tek forms property verbs/adjectives, as in kuttek 'black', sattek 'thin, emaciated', rettek 'decrepit, aged', and yautek 'cooled down'.","ja":"語尾 -tek は kuttek「黒い」、sattek「痩せた」、rettek「老衰した」、yautek「冷却した」のように形容詞（状態動詞）を形成する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-tek","kuttek","sattek","rettek","yautek"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0182-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-adjective-verb-p-se-means-heavy-but","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--candidate-counter-class"],"statement":{"en":"The adjective/verb páse means 'heavy', but it is also used with the meaning of 'noble / great'.","ja":"páse は「重い」という意味であるが、「偉い」という意味でも使われる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["páse"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0326-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-prefixes-ar-and-si-are-used-with","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--comparison-degree"],"statement":{"en":"The prefixes ar- and si- are used with stative verbs to intensify their meaning.","ja":"接頭辞 ar- および si- は状態動詞とともに用いられ、その意味を強意する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["with stative verbs"]},"forms":["ar-","si-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0172-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-prefix-ru-is-used-with-stative-verbs","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--comparison-degree"],"statement":{"en":"The prefix ru- is used with stative verbs to indicate a slight degree (e.g., sesek 'be warm' > rusesek 'be lukewarm').","ja":"接頭辞 ru- は状態動詞とともに用いられ、わずかな度合いを示す（例：sesek「温かい」> rusesek「ぬるい」）。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["with stative verbs"]},"forms":["ru-","sesek","rusesek"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0172-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-stative-verb-rupne-means-big-but-seems","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--comparison-degree"],"statement":{"en":"The stative verb rupne means 'big', but seems to carry the relative nuance of 'big among the same kind'.","ja":"rupne は「大きい」だが、「同種の中で大きい」という相対的な意味合いがあるようである。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["rupne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0374-02","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--verbal-affixes-like-the-causative-suffix-and-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--morphological-identity"],"statement":{"en":"Verbal affixes like the causative suffix and the applicative prefix attach equally to words with adjective-like meanings, provided they are semantically compatible.","ja":"使役接尾辞や適用接頭辞のような動詞接辞は、意味的に両立しうる限り、形容詞的な意味を持つ語にも同様に接続する。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"possible","conditions":["provided they are semantically compatible"]},"forms":["-re","-ka","e-","yay-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0091-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--in-sakhalin-ainu-asserted-forms-of-adjectives-are","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--morphological-identity"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, asserted forms of adjectives are formed identically to asserted forms of verbs using the auxiliary ki 'do'.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において、形容詞の断定形は動詞の断定形と同様に助動詞 ki「する」を用いて形成される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ki"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0020-05","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--in-ainu-asserted-forms-of-property-verbs-adjectives","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--morphological-identity"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu, asserted forms of property verbs (adjectives) are formed with the auxiliary verb ki 'do', just like verbs.","ja":"アイヌ語において形容詞（状態動詞）の主張形は動詞と同様に補助動詞 ki「する」を用いて形成される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ki"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0021-05","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--words-traditionally-classified-as-adjectives-can-undergo-causativization","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--morphological-identity"],"statement":{"en":"Words traditionally classified as adjectives can undergo causativization or transitivization by the addition of suffixes or prefixes like any other intransitive verb.","ja":"伝統的に形容詞と分類されてきた語は、他の自動詞と同様に、接尾辞や接頭辞の付加によって使役化または他動詞化され得る。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["wen","wente","pirka","pirkare","askay","easkay","peker","yaykouepekere"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0136-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--ainu-lacks-an-independent-adjective-word-class-concepts","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu lacks an independent adjective word class; concepts corresponding to adjectives are expressed by intransitive verbs.","ja":"アイヌ語には独立した形容詞という品詞がなく、形容詞に相当する概念は自動詞によって表される。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0002-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--adjectives-have-an-attributive-use-and-a-predicative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Adjectives have an attributive use and a predicative use.","ja":"形容詞には附加語的用法と述語的用法とがある。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0137-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--forms-corresponding-semantically-to-adjectives-in-other-languages","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Forms corresponding semantically to adjectives in other languages are treated as a subset of intransitive verbs, and 'adjectives' are not recognized as a separate word class.","ja":"他言語の形容詞に意味的に対応する形式は自動詞の一部として扱われ、「形容詞」は独立した品詞として立てられない。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0070-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--when-an-adjective-takes-personal-affixes-in-relation","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--person-marking-frame"],"statement":{"en":"When an adjective takes personal affixes in relation to a person, its conjugation completely matches that of Class II verbs.","ja":"形容詞が人格に関係して人称をとる時の活用は動詞の第II類と全く一致する。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["wen"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0106-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--all-adjectives-in-ainu-are-class-ii-verbs","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--person-marking-frame"],"statement":{"en":"All adjectives in Ainu are Class II verbs, so when the prefix e- attaches to an adjective, it shifts to a Class I transitive verb.","ja":"アイヌ語の形容詞はすべて第II類の動詞であり、したがってそれにe-が付加されれば当然第I類の他動詞に転ずる。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"all","modality":"necessary","conditions":["attaching to adjectives/stative verbs"]},"forms":["e-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0117-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--poro-means-large-big-but-in-certain-contexts","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--poro-pon"],"statement":{"en":"poro means 'large/big', but in certain contexts it can express the meaning 'adult, full-fledged, grown-up'.","ja":"poro は「大きい」という意味であるが、場合によっては「大人の、一人前の、成長した」という意味を表すことがある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["poro"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0369-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--ainu-lacks-a-separate-word-class-of-adjectives","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--standard-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu lacks a separate word class of adjectives, and property concepts such as pirka 'good' and pon 'small' are intransitive relative clause predicates.","ja":"アイヌ語には独立した形容詞品詞クラスが存在せず、pirka「良い」や pon「小さい」などの属性概念は自動詞の関係節述語である。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["pirka","pon"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0016-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--words-with-adjective-like-meanings-are-placed-directly","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--standard-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Words with adjective-like meanings are placed directly in predicate position without a copula.","ja":"形容詞的な意味を持つ語は、コピュラを伴わずにそのまま述語の位置に置かれる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["pon"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0091-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--words-with-adjective-like-meanings-modify-nouns-by","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--standard-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Words with adjective-like meanings modify nouns by preceding them with no morphological change, identically to verbs.","ja":"形容詞的な意味を持つ語は、動詞と同様に形態的変化を伴わずに名詞の前に置かれて修飾する。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0091-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--recognizing-an-independent-adjective-class-in-ainu-is","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--standard-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Recognizing an independent adjective class in Ainu is inappropriate because property-concept words show only minuscule differences from 1-valence verbs.","ja":"属性概念を表す語は1価動詞との差異がごく僅かであるため、アイヌ語において独立した形容詞品詞を設定することは不適切である。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0091-13","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--there-are-no-formal-or-distributional-differences-between","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--standard-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"There are no formal or distributional differences between 'adjectives' and intransitive verbs in Ainu, as both can occur in attributive and predicate position without change in form.","ja":"アイヌ語において「形容詞」と自動詞の間には形態的または分布上の違いはなく、いずれも形態変化を伴わずに連体修飾位置および述語位置に現れることができる。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0134-14","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--words-traditionally-classified-as-adjectives-exhibit-no-formal","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--standard-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Words traditionally classified as adjectives exhibit no formal or distributional differences from intransitive verbs, and both may occur in attributive and predicate positions without changes in form.","ja":"伝統的に形容詞と分類されてきた語は自動詞と形態的・分布的差異を示さず、両者ともに形態変化なしに連体修飾位置および述語位置に現れることができる。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0135-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--in-ainu-grammar-property-words-such-as-m","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--standard-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu grammar, property words such as méan 'be cold' are considered a type of verb, despite corresponding to adjectives in Japanese.","ja":"アイヌ語の文法では、méan「寒い」のような語は日本語の形容詞に相当するものの、動詞の一種と考えられる。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["méan"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0020-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--property-concept-words-corresponding-to-adjectives-function-as","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--standard-analysis"],"statement":{"en":"Property-concept words corresponding to adjectives function as predicates in the same manner as intransitive verbs, sharing personal affixes and adnominal modification syntax.","ja":"形容詞に相当する意味と機能を持つ語は自動詞とまったく同様に述語として機能し、同じ人称接辞を共有するだけでなく、名詞修飾語としても同一の振る舞いをする。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0018-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-verb-pirka-is-usually-translated-in-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--stative-inchoative"],"statement":{"en":"The verb 'pirka' is usually translated in a stative sense as 'good', but it can also be used in an inchoative sense as 'become good/recover'.","ja":"pirka は「良い」のように状態の意味に訳されるのが普通であるが，「良くなる」という変化の意味でも用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["pirka"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0037-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--the-verb-rupne-is-sometimes-used-to-mean","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topics":["topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs","topic:nominal/no-adjective-class-property-verbs--stative-inchoative"],"statement":{"en":"The verb rupne is sometimes used to mean 'to become an adult' or 'to grow old', as in rupne mat 'old woman'.","ja":"rupne は「大人になる，年を取る」という意味で用いられることがある（例：rupne mat「老婦人」）。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["rupne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0376-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
